## Q1 �?" Target and Fix Design (`P1`�?"`P10`, `P13`)

### Q1(a) Displacement mask and handler table (`P1`, `P2`, `P3`, `S7`, `S8`)
* **20-cell enumeration of `P1` (`READ` + `DERIVED`)**: Let `low_half = ((DS & 0x3fff) << 2) | XO`. Applying `(int16_t)(low_half & ~3)` clears bits `1:0` (`XO`) while leaving bit 15 of the halfword (bit 16 of `iword`, the sign bit of the 14-bit signed `DS` field) untouched:
  * `DS = -8192` (`0x2000`): `low_half = 0x8000 | XO` (`0x8000..0x8003`); `(int16_t)(low_half & ~3)` = `(int16_t)0x8000` = **`-32768`** for all `XO` $\in \{0,1,2,3\}$ (whereas unmasked `(int16_t)low_half` is `-32768, -32767, -32766, -32765`).
  * `DS = -1` (`0x3fff`): `low_half = 0xfffc | XO` (`0xfffc..0xffff`); `(int16_t)(low_half & ~3)` = `(int16_t)0xfffc` = **`-4`** for all `XO` $\in \{0,1,2,3\}$ (unmasked: `-4, -3, -2, -1`).
  * `DS = 0` (`0x0000`): `low_half = 0x0000 | XO` (`0x0000..0x0003`); `(int16_t)(low_half & ~3)` = `(int16_t)0x0000` = **`0`** for all `XO` $\in \{0,1,2,3\}$ (unmasked: `0, +1, +2, +3`).
  * `DS = +1` (`0x0001`): `low_half = 0x0004 | XO` (`0x0004..0x0007`); `(int16_t)(low_half & ~3)` = `(int16_t)0x0004` = **`+4`** for all `XO` $\in \{0,1,2,3\}$ (unmasked: `+4, +5, +6, +7`).
  * `DS = +8191` (`0x1fff`): `low_half = 0x7ffc | XO` (`0x7ffc..0x7fff`); `(int16_t)(low_half & ~3)` = `(int16_t)0x7ffc` = **`+32764`** for all `XO` $\in \{0,1,2,3\}$ (unmasked: `+32764, +32765, +32766, +32767`).
  Widening `(ssize_t)(int16_t)(iword & ~3)` into `ic->arg[2]` ([cpu_ppc_instr.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr.c#L4351)) and reading `(int32_t)ic->arg[2]` in [`LS_GENERIC_N`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr_loadstore.c#L42) (`READ`) preserves the exact signed 16-bit value `EXTS(DS || 0b00)` across all 20 cells.
* **Handler table check of `P3` (`READ`)**: Opened [generate_ppc_loadstore.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/generate_ppc_loadstore.c#L40-L83), [tmp_ppc_loadstore.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/tmp_ppc_loadstore.c#L893-L958), and [cpu_ppc_instr_loadstore.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr_loadstore.c#L113-L186). The index at [cpu_ppc_instr.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr.c#L4331-L4336) is `size + 4*zero + 8*load + (imm==0? 16 : 0) + 32*update`:
  * `58/0` (`ld`): `load=1, size=3, zero=1, update=0` $\rightarrow$ slots `15` (`ppc_instr_ld`) / `31` (`ppc_instr_ld_0`), 64-bit load (`LS_D`), no update.
  * `58/1` (`ldu`): `load=1, size=3, zero=1, update=1` $\rightarrow$ slots `47` (`ppc_instr_ldu`) / `63` (`ppc_instr_ldu_0`), 64-bit load (`LS_D`), `reg(ic->arg[1]) = addr` at [cpu_ppc_instr_loadstore.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr_loadstore.c#L183-L185).
  * `58/2` (`lwa`): `load=1, size=2, zero=0, update=0` $\rightarrow$ slots `10` (`ppc_instr_lwa`) / `26` (`ppc_instr_lwa_0`). At [cpu_ppc_instr_loadstore.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr_loadstore.c#L120-L125) (`READ`), `LS_W` without `LS_ZERO` computes `(int32_t)((data[0] << 24) + (data[1] << 16) + (data[2] << 8) + data[3])` and assigns it to `uint64_t` `reg(ic->arg[0])`, sign-extending bit 31 through `0..31`.
  * `62/0` (`std`): `load=0, size=3, zero=1` (or `0`) `, update=0` $\rightarrow$ slots `7`/`23` (or `3`/`19`, both holding `ppc_instr_std` / `ppc_instr_std_0`), 64-bit store (`LS_D`), no update.
  * `62/1` (`stdu`): `load=0, size=3, zero=1` (or `0`) `, update=1` $\rightarrow$ slots `39`/`55` (or `35`/`51`, both holding `ppc_instr_stdu` / `ppc_instr_stdu_0`), 64-bit store (`LS_D`), `reg(ic->arg[1]) = addr` after `memory_rw`.
  * `ppc_instr_invalid` ([cpu_ppc_instr.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr.c#L241-L245) `READ`) occupies only the four `load=1, zero=0, size=3` slots (`11, 27, 43, 59`). None of the five legal DS-forms sets both `size=3` and `zero=0` (`lwa` sets `size=2, zero=0`; `ld`/`ldu` keep `zero=1`). No handler changes are needed.

### Q1(b) Ordering of the `imm` mask relative to `imm == 0` (`P2`)
* **Where `imm` is read (`READ`)**: In [`X(to_be_translated)`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr.c#L4295-L4351), `imm` is read twice:
  1. Line 4335: `(imm==0? 16 : 0)` inside the `ppc_loadstore[...]` index.
  2. Line 4351: `ic->arg[2] = (ssize_t)imm;`.
* **Exact inputs where raw vs. masked `imm == 0` disagree (`DERIVED` from `P2`)**: They disagree **if and only if `DS == 0` and `XO != 0`** (the three legal zero-displacement non-zero-XO cells: `ldu` with `DS=0` [`C5`, raw `imm = 1`], `lwa` with `DS=0` [`C10`, raw `imm = 2`], and `stdu` with `DS=0` [`C16`, raw `imm = 1`]). When `DS != 0`, both raw and masked `imm` are non-zero; when `XO == 0`, raw equals masked.
* **Effect of `_0` vs non-`_0` handlers (`READ`)**: Opened [cpu_ppc_instr_loadstore.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr_loadstore.c#L41-L54) and [cpu_ppc_instr_loadstore.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr_loadstore.c#L195-L216).
  * On a **64-bit CPU** (`!cpu->is_32bit`), [`LS_N`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr_loadstore.c#L195-L198) immediately calls `LS_GENERIC_N(cpu, ic)` and returns. Because `LS_GENERIC_N` is emitted only once per `(size, zero, load, update)` tuple under `#ifndef LS_IGNOREOFS` ([generate_ppc_loadstore.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/generate_ppc_loadstore.c#L62-L82) `READ`), `ppc_instr_ldu_0` and `ppc_instr_ldu` call the same `ppc_generic_ldu`, which always adds `(int32_t)ic->arg[2]`.
  * On a **32-bit CPU** (`MODE32`, which reaches these handlers when opcodes 58/62 are not gated by `bits == 32`), the fast path in [`LS_N`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr_loadstore.c#L202-L215) (`READ`) omits `+ (int32_t)ic->arg[2]` when `LS_IGNOREOFS` (`_0`) is selected and adds `+ (int32_t)ic->arg[2]` when non-`_0` is selected.
* **Design requirement**: Assigning `imm = (int16_t)(iword & ~3);` inside `case PPC_HI6_LD:` ([cpu_ppc_instr.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr.c#L4307)) and `case PPC_HI6_STD:` ([cpu_ppc_instr.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr.c#L4320)) naturally precedes line 4328 (`if (ic->f == NULL)`), so both `(imm==0? 16 : 0)` at line 4335 and `ic->arg[2] = (ssize_t)imm` at line 4351 see the masked `imm`. The design record must state explicitly that `imm` is masked inside `PPC_HI6_LD`/`PPC_HI6_STD` before line 4328.

### Q1(c) Illegal `XO` handling (`58/3`, `62/2`, `62/3`) and `R12` (`P6`, `S5`, `S6`, `R12`)
* **Verification of `P6` (`READ`)**: Opened [cpu_ppc.h](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/include/cpu_ppc.h#L251-L257) and [cpu_ppc_instr.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr.c#L4141-L5433). Only `PPC_EXCEPTION_DSI`, `ISI`, `EXT`, `DEC`, `SC`, and `FPU` are defined; neither `0x700` (Program) nor `0x600` (Alignment) exists in the tree.
* **`R12` classification (`DERIVED`)**: Because architectural Program exception (`5 FAULT`) does not exist on this CPU (`R12` availability rule; `S5`, `P6`), `goto bad` is the fork's decoder-level refusal idiom (**`3 DECLINE + BOUNDED ANNOUNCE`** coupled with halting execution via `cpu->running = 0` at [`bad:`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_dyntrans.c#L2004-L2015) `READ`). Because `bad:` sets `cpu->running = 0` on the first hit (`S6`, `P15`), the announcement (`"UNIMPLEMENTED instruction at 0x..."`) is inherently bounded to one emission per run without a static latch.
* **Bare `goto bad` vs. `fatal()` before `goto bad` (`READ`)**: Checked every `goto bad` site in [`X(to_be_translated)`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr.c#L4531-L5426) (`READ`):
  * All unrecognized/reserved primary and extended opcode switches�?"`PPC_HI6_19` (`:4531`), `PPC_HI6_30` (`:4609`), `PPC_HI6_31` (`:5172`), `PPC_HI6_59` (`:5218`), `PPC_HI6_63` (`:5410`), and outer `default:` (`:5426`)�?"use **bare `default: goto bad;`** with no extra `fatal()` call, letting `bad:` in `cpu_dyntrans.c` print the standard `"UNIMPLEMENTED instruction"` line and disassembly when `!cpu->translation_readahead`.
  * Pre-`goto bad` `fatal("TODO: ...")` calls (`:4340`, `:4604`, `:4815`, `:4997`) are used only for valid architectural features not yet implemented. Reserved/illegal `XO` values (`58/3`, `62/2`, `62/3`) are invalid instruction forms (`S2`, `S4`), so **bare `default: goto bad;`** is the exact fork idiom.

### Q1(d) Register-constraint invalid forms: `RA = 0` and `RA = RT` / `RA = RS` (`P4`, `P5`, `D1`)
* **`ldu` and `stdu` with `RA = 0` (`P5`, `C6`, `C17` �?" `READ`)**: Setting `update = 1` for `58/1` (`ldu`) and `62/1` (`stdu`) feeds the existing guard at [cpu_ppc_instr.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr.c#L4338-L4342) (`if (ra == 0 && update) { if (!cpu->translation_readahead) fatal("TODO: ra=0 && update?\n"); goto bad; }` `READ`). Turning pre-fix execution at absolute address `EXTS(DS || 01)` without update into `goto bad` is **right** and matches every other D-form (`lbzu`, `lhzu`, `lhau`, `lwzu`, `lfsu`, `lfdu`, `stbu`, `sthu`, `stwu`, `stfsu`, `stfdu` at `:4338`) and X-form (`:4995`) update instruction in the file.
* **`ldu` with `RA = RT != 0` (`P4`, `D1`, `C7` �?" `READ`)**: Ruling on `D1`: **"disclosed, not checked"** (Grok / `CRIT_RULINGS.md` position) is right and does not change the design.
  * In [cpu_ppc_instr.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr.c#L4298-L4352) and [cpu_ppc_instr_loadstore.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr_loadstore.c#L128-L185) (`READ`), none of the existing integer update loads (`lbzu`, `lhzu`, `lhau`, `lwzu`, `lhaux`, `lwzux`, `lbzux`) checks `ra == rt`; when `ra == rt`, `LS_GENERIC_N` writes the loaded value to `*(uint64_t *)(ic->arg[0])` (`gpr[rt]`) at line 130 and then overwrites `reg(ic->arg[1])` (`gpr[ra]`) with `addr` (`EA`) at line 184. Under Power ISA Book I (`S3`), `RA = RT` is an invalid form whose architectural outcome is boundedly undefined (`RT` receiving `EA` is a standard hardware outcome).
* **`stdu` with `RA = RS != 0` (`P4`, `C18` �?" `READ`)**: Book I (`S4`) permits `RA = RS` on `stdu`. In [`LS_GENERIC_N`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr_loadstore.c#L163-L185) (`READ`), `uint64_t x = *(uint64_t *)(ic->arg[0])` (`gpr[rs]`) is packed into `data[0..7]` and written via `cpu->memory_rw` (lines 165�?"174) **before** `reg(ic->arg[1]) = addr` updates `gpr[ra]` (line 184). Because the repair does not reject `ra == rs`, `stdu` with `RA = RS != 0` stores the old `RS` value and updates `RA` to `EA`.

### Q1(e) 64-bit-only instructions on 32-bit CPUs (`P7`, `D2`, `S9`, `S11`, `S12`, `R13`, `R17`)
* **Audit of `P7` across [`X(to_be_translated)`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr.c#L4141-L5433) (`READ`)**:
  * **Gated on `cpu->cd.ppc.bits == 32`**: Only `PPC_HI6_30` (`rld*`) at [cpu_ppc_instr.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr.c#L4602-L4606) (`READ`).
  * **Ungated 64-bit-only instructions decoded in `X(to_be_translated)` (`READ`)**: `cmpdi`/`cmpldi` (`l_bit == 1` at `:4185`, `:4191`, `:4624`, `:4629`), `PPC_HI6_LD` (`:4307`), `PPC_HI6_STD` (`:4320`), `PPC_19_RFID` (`:4500`), `PPC_31_MTMSRD` (`:4705`), `PPC_31_LDARX` (`:4867`), `PPC_31_STDCX_DOT` (`:4869`), `PPC_31_STDX` (`:4921`), `PPC_31_STDUX` (`:4922`), `PPC_31_EXTSW` (`:5004`), and `PPC_31_SLD` (`:5006`).
  * **Other 64-bit-only instructions (`READ`)**: `PPC_HI6_TDI` (`opcodes_ppc.h:61`) and `PPC_31_TD` (`opcodes_ppc.h:97`) are disassembled in `cpu_ppc.c:892, 958` (`READ`) but absent from `X(to_be_translated)` (hitting `default: goto bad;`); `ldx`, `ldux`, `lwax`, `lwaux`, `mulld`, `divd`, `srd`, `srad`, and `cntlzd` have no `PPC_31_*` defines in [opcodes_ppc.h](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/include/opcodes_ppc.h) (`READ`) and also fall into `default: goto bad;`.
* **Choice between `(i)` and `(ii)` on `D2` (`DERIVED` under `R13`, `R17`)**: **Choose `(i)` �?" disclose in `NOT CLAIMED` (`C24`), do not add a `bits == 32` gate in this round** (consistent with Grok and `CRIT_RULINGS.md`).
  * *Why*: Twelve 64-bit-only forms in `X(to_be_translated)` (including sibling X-form `stdx`, `stdux`, `ldarx`, `stdcx.`) are ungated on 32-bit CPUs (`P7`). Adding `if (cpu->cd.ppc.bits == 32) goto bad;` to opcodes 58/62 alone is outside the round's witness (`bareppc` / `PPC970`) and would leave `stdx`/`stdux` inconsistent, whereas gating all twelve belongs to a dedicated 32-bit-mode illegal-64-bit-opcode round (`R17`).

### Q1(f) Alignment of `EA` (`P8`, `S14`)
* **Verification of `P8` (`READ`)**: Opened [cpu_ppc_instr_loadstore.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr_loadstore.c#L41-L198) and [memory_ppc.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/memory_ppc.c#L254-L296). On 64-bit CPUs (`!cpu->is_32bit`), [`LS_N`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr_loadstore.c#L195-L198) always delegates to [`LS_GENERIC_N`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr_loadstore.c#L41-L186), which computes `uint64_t addr = reg(ic->arg[1]) + (int32_t)ic->arg[2];` and passes `addr` directly to `cpu->memory_rw` with `LS_SIZE` (`4` or `8`) and no alignment check (open items `#430`/`#431`). Even on 32-bit CPUs where the fast path checks `ofs & (LS_SIZE - 1)` ([cpu_ppc_instr_loadstore.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr_loadstore.c#L229)), an unaligned address simply falls back to `LS_GENERIC_N` (`:230`).
* **Conclusion**: Nothing in the repair or its handlers assumes a 4- or 8-byte-aligned `EA` (`RA` may hold any byte address; the displacement `EXTS(DS || 0b00)` is always a multiple of 4). Using `BASE = 0x20080` in the probe is purely a test-data choice.

### Q1(g) Disassembler folding in [`ppc_cpu_disassemble_instr`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc.c#L1468-L1601) (`P10`, `R16`, `R17`, `C25`)
* **Verification of `P10` (`READ`)**: Opened [cpu_ppc.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc.c#L1468-L1601) and [debugger_cmds.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/debugger/debugger_cmds.c#L1837-L1947).
  * At [cpu_ppc.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc.c#L1495-L1525), `ppc_cpu_disassemble_instr` computes `imm = (int16_t)(iword & 0xffff);`, assigns `mnem = "ld"` for `PPC_HI6_LD` (`:1498`) and `mnem = "std"` for `PPC_HI6_STD` (`:1517`), never inspects `iword & 3`, and prints `debug("%s\tr%i,%i(r%i)", mnem, rt, imm, ra)` (`:1532`). (Notably, `PPC_HI6_LFSU`, `LFDU`, `STFSU`, `STFDU` are also missing from the `case` list at `:1477-1489`!)
  * When invoked from debugger `unassemble` (`cpu->running == 0`, [debugger_cmds.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/debugger/debugger_cmds.c#L1928)), `ppc_cpu_disassemble_instr` returns early at [cpu_ppc.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc.c#L1535-L1536) without touching guest memory. When invoked during live instruction tracing (`cpu->running == 1`), it performs a debug-only `cpu->memory_rw(..., MEM_READ, NO_EXCEPTIONS)` preview (`:1549-1550`) that does not alter guest registers or memory.
* **Ruling (`R16`, `R17`)**: **File separately (do not fold into `#571`)**.
  * Under `R17`, a second site in a different file ([cpu_ppc.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc.c)) with a guest-invisible cosmetic symptom (`LOW`) should not be bundled when doing so would invalidate the witness's green `unasm census` oracle (`R16`).
  * With the disassembler filed separately, `regress/ppc_dsform_probe.py`'s `CONTRACT` must state explicitly under `OBSERVED` / `NOT CLAIMED` that `unasm census` verifies word placement (`opcd`, `RT`/`RS`, `RA`, and raw `DS || XO` halfword) against the tree's current `ld`/`std`-folding disassembler and **does not attest `XO` decode** (`C25`).

