## Q2 �?" Detector Row Set and Floor (`P9`, `P11`�?"`P15`, `C1`�?"`C26`, `R1`�?"`R11`, `R15`�?"`R19`)

### Q2(a) Store half (`PPC_HI6_STD` = 62) (`P9`, `R1` clause (a))
* **Verification of `P9` (`READ`)**: In [cpu_ppc_instr.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr.c#L4295-L4327) (`READ`), `case PPC_HI6_STD: size = 3; load = 0; break;` leaves `update = 0` and `imm = (int16_t)iword` for every `XO` $\in \{0,1,2,3\}$. Therefore on `BASE` (HEAD):
  * `62/0` (`std`): stores 8 bytes of `RS` at `EA`, leaves `RA` unchanged (**GREEN** on `BASE`).
  * `62/1` (`stdu`): stores 8 bytes of `RS` at `EA + 1` and leaves `RA` unchanged (**RED** on `BASE`).
  * `62/1` (`stdu` with `RA = 0`, `C17`): stores 8 bytes of `RS` at absolute address `EXTS(DS || 01)` instead of `goto bad` (**RED** on `BASE`).
  * `62/1` (`stdu` with `RA = RS != 0`, `C18`): stores 8 bytes of `RS` at `EA + 1` and leaves `RA` unchanged (**RED** on `BASE`).
  * `62/2` and `62/3` (`C19`, `C20`): store 8 bytes of `RS` at `EA + 2` and `EA + 3` instead of `goto bad` (**RED** on `BASE`).
* **Store rows and observables owed before the fix lands**:
  1. **`std value` & `std RA after` (`C13`, control, `DS != 0`, e.g. `DS = -2`, `EA = BASE - 8`)**: store an 8-distinct-byte register value (e.g. `0xa0a1a2a3a4a5a6a7`) into a pre-seeded scratch region; verify via debugger `dump` that `MEM(EA, 8) == 0xa0a1a2a3a4a5a6a7` and neighbouring bytes `MEM(EA - 4, 4)` and `MEM(EA + 8, 4)` retain their pre-seeded background bytes, and verify `RA == BASE` (`std RA after`).
  2. **`stdu value`, `stdu neigh`, & `stdu RA after` (`C15`, symptom, `DS != 0`, e.g. `DS = +4`, `EA = BASE + 16`)**: store an 8-distinct-byte value (e.g. `0xb0b1b2b3b4b5b6b7`); verify via debugger `dump` that `MEM(EA, 8) == 0xb0b1b2b3b4b5b6b7` (**RED** on `BASE`, where byte `EA` is still the background seed and `0xb0..b6` land at `EA+1..EA+7`), verify that neighbour window `MEM(EA + 8, 4)` retains its pre-seeded background (**RED** on `BASE`, where byte `EA + 8` is overwritten with `0xb7`), and verify `RA == EA` (`stdu RA after`, **RED** on `BASE` where `RA == BASE`).
  3. **`stdu ds0 value` (`C16`, symptom, `DS = 0`, `EA = BASE`)**: store an 8-distinct-byte value at `DS = 0`; verify `MEM(BASE, 8)` holds the stored doubleword and `MEM(BASE + 8, 1)` is untouched (**RED** on `BASE`, which writes to `BASE + 1..BASE + 8`).
  4. **`stdu alias value` & `stdu alias RA after` (`C18`, symptom, `RA = RS != 0`, `DS != 0`)**: with `rA = BASE`, execute `stdu rA, DS(rA)`; verify `MEM(EA, 8) == BASE` (old `rA`) and post-instruction `rA == EA` (**RED** on `BASE`).
  5. **`stdu ra0 bad` (`C17`, symptom, `RA = 0`, in its own session)**: verify `"UNIMPLEMENTED instruction"` in transcript and target memory at `EXTS(DS || 01)` untouched (**RED** on `BASE`).
  6. **`b62_2 bad` (`C19`) and `b62_3 bad` (`C20`, symptoms, each in its own session)**: verify `"UNIMPLEMENTED instruction"` in transcript, `RA == BASE`, and `MEM(EA, 12)` (covering `EA..EA+11`, which includes `EA+2..EA+9` and `EA+3..EA+10`) still equals the pre-seeded background (**RED** on `BASE`).

### Q2(b) Reversing the fix (`P13`, `P15`, `R1` clause (b))
* **Verification of `P13` and `P15` (`READ`)**: The repair touches only the displacement assignment and `case PPC_HI6_LD:` / `case PPC_HI6_STD:` in [cpu_ppc_instr.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr.c#L4295-L4327).
* When HEAD's code is reinstated at those sites:
  * In the main non-stopping session, HEAD never takes `goto bad` on any legal `ld`, `ldu`, `lwa`, `std`, or `stdu` with `RA != 0`, so the session runs all the way through `live` (`li r26, 0x42`), and every symptom row (`ldu value`, `ldu RA after`, `ldu ds0 value`, `lwa value`, `lwa pos value`, `lwa ds0 value`, `stdu value`, `stdu neigh`, `stdu RA after`, `stdu ds0 value`, `stdu alias value`, `stdu alias RA after`) fails on its own register/memory value while all controls (`ld`, `std`, `lwz`, `C21`, `C22`, `live`, `unasm census`, `neg apparatus`) stay GREEN (`CONTROL=OK`, `SYMPTOM=PRESENT`).
  * In each of the five dedicated `goto bad` sessions (`C6`, `C12`, `C17`, `C19`, `C20`), placing the liveness `li` **before** the illegal word (`P15`) ensures that on the fixed build the liveness row is GREEN and the illegal word halts with `"UNIMPLEMENTED instruction"`, whereas on reinstated HEAD the illegal word executes as a shifted `ld`/`std` without halting, turning the session's `bad` row RED while its `live` row remains GREEN.

### Q2(c) Clause (c) �?" Identity-body and dead-binary checks (`R2`)
* **Medium & record form (`R2`)**: Run and record an **identity-body mutant** (`(c): measured at <artifact>`) in the pass-2 kill table�?"where `PPC_HI6_LD` and `PPC_HI6_STD` decode and advance `pc` without reading/writing memory or modifying `RT`/`RA`�?"plus state the by-construction dead-binary prediction:
  * **On the identity-body mutant (`DERIVED`)**: Every register stays at `SENT` (`0x5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a`) or `BASE` (`0x20080`) and scratch memory stays at its pre-seeded pattern. Therefore:
    * Controls `ld value` (`0x5a5a.. != 0x1011..`) and `std value` (background `!= 0xa0a1..`) go **RED**, flipping `PPC_DSFORM_CONTROL=FAIL`.
    * Symptoms `ldu value`, `ldu RA after`, `ldu ds0 value`, `lwa value`, `lwa pos value`, `lwa ds0 value`, `stdu value`, `stdu RA after`, `stdu ds0 value`, `stdu alias value`, `stdu alias RA after`, and all five `goto bad` stop-transcript checks (`C6`, `C12`, `C17`, `C19`, `C20`) go **RED**.
  * **On a dead binary (`READ` from [ppc_dsform_probe.py](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/ppcdsformxo/witness_20261024/ppc_dsform_probe.py#L444-L470))**:
    * If the binary exits immediately without running debugger commands (`regs == {}`, `dis == []`), `unasm census` compares `"%d/%d" % (matched, len(dis))` (`"0/0"`) against `"%d/%d" % (N, N)` and goes **RED** (note: `unasm census` *does* depend on the emulator running `unassemble` in the main session, so it is only green on the identity-body mutant, not on a dead binary).
    * On `/bin/false` (`exit 1` with empty output), `neg apparatus` (`"exit1/-0x1"`) is the sole row that can match (`1/N`), while `PPC_DSFORM_RESULT`, `PPC_DSFORM_CONTROL=FAIL`, and all `N-1` other rows fail; on `/bin/true` (`exit 0`), `neg apparatus` (`"exit0/-0x1" != "exit1/-0x1"`) also goes **RED** (`0/N`).

