### Q2(e) Classifying the named variants and preserving non-target instructions (`P14`)
1. *"Displacement masked but `update` left 0 (`RA` unchanged)"*: **`(d)` null mutant** of the `update = 1` assignment on `58/1` (`ldu`) or `62/1` (`stdu`). Killed by `ldu RA after` (`C4`) and `stdu RA after` (`C15`) at `DS != 0`.
2. *"`update` set but raw `int16_t` kept (access at `EA + 1`)"*: **`(d)` null mutant** of the `imm & ~3` mask on `58/1` or `62/1`. Killed by `ldu value` (`C4`), `ldu RA after` (`C4`), `ldu ds0 value` (`C5`), `stdu value` (`C15`), `stdu RA after` (`C15`), and `stdu ds0 value` (`C16`).
3. *"`lwa` left at `size = 3` (neighbour word consumed)"*: **`(d)` null mutant** of `size = 2; zero = 0;` on `58/2`. Killed by `lwa value` (`C8`), `lwa pos value` (`C9`), and `lwa ds0 value` (`C10`).
4. *"A growth mutant that adds 1 to `XO=0` reds that row"* (or sets `update = 1` on `XO = 0` / `lwa`):
