2733: **R2 -- clause (c): the null medium by instrument kind, the pre-fix build, the two record forms** -- lines 1340-1367, VERBATIM:
2734: ~~~~
2735: 1340| > **ONE criterion -- a product medium carrying none of the behaviour under test -- and its object
2736: 1341| > differs by instrument kind:**
2737: 1342| > * an offline differential that `#include`s the product: a COMMENT-ONLY product source, which must
2738: 1343| >   fail to COMPILE, with a gate that reds on the compile failure (measured for `#488`:
2739: 1344| >   `regress/artifacts/shortread/nullmedium_20261009/RECEIPT.txt`);
2740: 1345| > * a runtime probe: an ABSENT or NON-EMULATOR binary (every session dies), or a build WITHOUT the
2741: 1346| >   device for a device round;
2742: 1347| > * an instruction-handler round: an IDENTITY BODY (decode and retire, write nothing) -- the
2743: 1348| >   recommended default, two measured legs at `#527`.
2744: 1349| >
2745: 1350| > **THE PRE-FIX BUILD IS CLAUSE (a)'S MEDIUM AND NEVER CLAUSE (c)'S.**  It carries every behaviour of the
2746: 1351| > product, one of them wrong, so a detector can red on it and still pass a comment-only file -- `#446`,
2747: 1352| > the instance that created this clause.  A table that wrote "null medium" over a pre-fix leg carries a
2748: 1353| > WRONG RECORD (L4: correct it in place, quoting what it refutes, as
2749: 1354| > `ppcrldimimask/killtable_20260911/SCORES.txt` does), NOT a floor breach: clause (c) is then
2750: 1355| > UNMEASURED there.  **A breach is a genuine null medium coming back GREEN, and nothing else** -- "a
2751: 1356| > sharper medium was available" is not a floor criterion (at most clause-(e) debt).
2752: 1357| >
2753: 1358| > **RECORD CLAUSE (c) IN ONE OF EXACTLY TWO FORMS, never as a bare clause letter beside a row name:**
2754: 1359| > * `(c): measured at <artifact>` -- the leg was run and its receipt is durable;
2755: 1360| > * `(c): by construction via <row/pin>, leg not run` -- e.g. the gate pins the row count by EQUALITY
2756: 1361| >   and a named row reds on a dead run, or the differential `#include`s the product and its gate reds
2757: 1362| >   on a compile failure.  **A by-construction claim is checked by READING that shape; where the reading
2758: 1363| >   fails -- no runtime gate wiring, no pin, `check_min`, a control computed over the row list
2759: 1364| >   (`all([])` is True) -- the leg is OWED** (7n-1's two: the unwired `ppc_rldicl_probe.py` and
2760: 1365| >   `alpha_tbi_probe.py`).  Predict a dead run's score from the source, not from the row count (Astra
2761: 1366| >   measured luna's at 0/14 with four gate checks red, and SGI's at 6/46 because six rows test only
2762: 1367| >   exit status).
