 489: **3.3 Grok 4.7's T2 answer -- `grok_crit.txt` Q3, VERBATIM:**
 490: ~~~~
 491: 44| ## Q3. T2 �?" mask the DS XO; five legal forms; no alignment exception; nothing to port
 492: 45| 
 493: 46| `cpu_ppc_instr.c:4295` takes `imm = (int16_t)iword` and `:4307` / `:4320` treat primary opcodes `0x3a` and `0x3e` as one form each: 8 bytes, no update. Book I (the local `ppc_uisa_book1_v201` text) gives XO in bits 30:31 and the displacement as `EXTS(DS || 0b00)`.
 494: 47| 
 495: 48| For every legal XO, `imm = (int16_t)(iword & ~3)`.
 496: 49| 
 497: 50| | opcode | XO | form | width | update |
 498: 51| |---|---|---|---|---|
 499: 52| | 58 | 0 | `ld` | 8, zero-extend | no |
 500: 53| | 58 | 1 | `ldu` | 8 | yes |
 501: 54| | 58 | 2 | `lwa` | 4, sign-extend (`size=2`, `zero=0`; the cast is `cpu_ppc_instr_loadstore.c:119-120`) | no |
 502: 55| | 62 | 0 | `std` | 8 | no |
 503: 56| | 62 | 1 | `stdu` | 8 | yes |
 504: 57| 
 505: 58| `ldu` with RA=0 already hits `:4338-4341` (`goto bad`) once `update` is set. `ldu` with RA=RT is invalid in Book I and is not checked. This round does not add that check: the only refusal on hand is `goto bad`, a CPU-stop, and this tree's exception list (`cpu_ppc.h:252-257`) has no program exception. Left disclosed. Reserved XO (58/3, 62/2, 62/3) must not fall through as `ld`/`std`. They take the same `goto bad` an unrecognized opcode already takes. One row: opcode 58 with XO=3 does not load 8 bytes and does not update RA.
 506: 59| 
 507: 60| Unaligned accesses stay as `#431` left them. `cpu_ppc_instr_loadstore.c` performs the access; there is no PPC alignment vector. The EA+1 store is the decoder, and it disappears once the low two bits are masked. A genuinely unaligned EA (RA not a multiple of 8, DS a multiple of 4) is still performed. Do not port rs6000 `9a05a7b`. The same arms fire on 32-bit CPUs, where 58/62 are not the 32-bit ISA. Disclosed, not fixed here. XO=0 `ld`/`std` are already right and are the accept side.
 508: 61| 
 509: 62| The witness runs with MSR IR and DR clear. On PPC970 a translated access dies in the N3 exit before the store is observable. `testppc` defaults to PPC970 (`machine_test.c:450`). With translation off, `memory_ppc.c:258-261` is the identity map.
 510: 63| 
 511: 64| Floor: (a) `stdu` with XO=1, DS nonzero, RA�%�0, 8-aligned EA, stores at EA+1 and leaves RA unchanged. (b) Restore `(int16_t)iword` and `update=0` for opcode 62. (c) Identity body: decode, retire, memory and RA unchanged. (d) Three nulls of the same guard: displacement masked but `update` left 0 (RA unchanged); `update` set but the raw `int16_t` kept (store at EA+1); `lwa` left at `size=3` (the neighbour word is consumed). Accept: XO=0 `std` still stores the whole doubleword at EA and does not write RA. A growth mutant that adds 1 to XO=0 reds that row. `lwa` oracle: a negative word, sign-extended, the next 4 bytes a sentinel.
 512: 65| 
 513: 66| Rung-3: cold debugger, unmodified `testppc`, translation off, real decode, real `memory_rw` into RAM. One `stdu`, one `ldu`, one `lwa`, one XO=0 `std`. Liveness is an `stw` of a known word.
