  38: ### Q1(c) Illegal `XO` handling (`58/3`, `62/2`, `62/3`) and `R12` (`P6`, `S5`, `S6`, `R12`)
  39: * **Verification of `P6` (`READ`)**: Opened [cpu_ppc.h](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/include/cpu_ppc.h#L251-L257) and [cpu_ppc_instr.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr.c#L4141-L5433). Only `PPC_EXCEPTION_DSI`, `ISI`, `EXT`, `DEC`, `SC`, and `FPU` are defined; neither `0x700` (Program) nor `0x600` (Alignment) exists in the tree.
  40: * **`R12` classification (`DERIVED`)**: Because architectural Program exception (`5 FAULT`) does not exist on this CPU (`R12` availability rule; `S5`, `P6`), `goto bad` is the fork's decoder-level refusal idiom (**`3 DECLINE + BOUNDED ANNOUNCE`** coupled with halting execution via `cpu->running = 0` at [`bad:`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_dyntrans.c#L2004-L2015) `READ`). Because `bad:` sets `cpu->running = 0` on the first hit (`S6`, `P15`), the announcement (`"UNIMPLEMENTED instruction at 0x..."`) is inherently bounded to one emission per run without a static latch.
  41: * **Bare `goto bad` vs. `fatal()` before `goto bad` (`READ`)**: Checked every `goto bad` site in [`X(to_be_translated)`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr.c#L4531-L5426) (`READ`):
  42:   * All unrecognized/reserved primary and extended opcode switches-`PPC_HI6_19` (`:4531`), `PPC_HI6_30` (`:4609`), `PPC_HI6_31` (`:5172`), `PPC_HI6_59` (`:5218`), `PPC_HI6_63` (`:5410`), and outer `default:` (`:5426`)-use **bare `default: goto bad;`** with no extra `fatal()` call, letting `bad:` in `cpu_dyntrans.c` print the standard `"UNIMPLEMENTED instruction"` line and disassembly when `!cpu->translation_readahead`.
  43:   * Pre-`goto bad` `fatal("TODO: ...")` calls (`:4340`, `:4604`, `:4815`, `:4997`) are used only for valid architectural features not yet implemented. Reserved/illegal `XO` values (`58/3`, `62/2`, `62/3`) are invalid instruction forms (`S2`, `S4`), so **bare `default: goto bad;`** is the exact fork idiom.
  44: 
  45: ### Q1(d) Register-constraint invalid forms: `RA = 0` and `RA = RT` / `RA = RS` (`P4`, `P5`, `D1`)
  46: * **`ldu` and `stdu` with `RA = 0` (`P5`, `C6`, `C17` - `READ`)**: Setting `update = 1` for `58/1` (`ldu`) and `62/1` (`stdu`) feeds the existing guard at [cpu_ppc_instr.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr.c#L4338-L4342) (`if (ra == 0 && update) { if (!cpu->translation_readahead) fatal("TODO: ra=0 && update?\n"); goto bad; }` `READ`). Turning pre-fix execution at absolute address `EXTS(DS || 01)` without update into `goto bad` is **right** and matches every other D-form (`lbzu`, `lhzu`, `lhau`, `lwzu`, `lfsu`, `lfdu`, `stbu`, `sthu`, `stwu`, `stfsu`, `stfdu` at `:4338`) and X-form (`:4995`) update instruction in the file.
  47: * **`ldu` with `RA = RT != 0` (`P4`, `D1`, `C7` - `READ`)**: Ruling on `D1`: **"disclosed, not checked"** (Grok / `CRIT_RULINGS.md` position) is right and does not change the design.
  48:   * In [cpu_ppc_instr.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr.c#L4298-L4352) and [cpu_ppc_instr_loadstore.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr_loadstore.c#L128-L185) (`READ`), none of the existing integer update loads (`lbzu`, `lhzu`, `lhau`, `lwzu`, `lhaux`, `lwzux`, `lbzux`) checks `ra == rt`; when `ra == rt`, `LS_GENERIC_N` writes the loaded value to `*(uint64_t *)(ic->arg[0])` (`gpr[rt]`) at line 130 and then overwrites `reg(ic->arg[1])` (`gpr[ra]`) with `addr` (`EA`) at line 184. Under Power ISA Book I (`S3`), `RA = RT` is an invalid form whose architectural outcome is boundedly undefined (`RT` receiving `EA` is a standard hardware outcome).
  49: * **`stdu` with `RA = RS != 0` (`P4`, `C18` - `READ`)**: Book I (`S4`) permits `RA = RS` on `stdu`. In [`LS_GENERIC_N`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr_loadstore.c#L163-L185) (`READ`), `uint64_t x = *(uint64_t *)(ic->arg[0])` (`gpr[rs]`) is packed into `data[0..7]` and written via `cpu->memory_rw` (lines 165-174) **before** `reg(ic->arg[1]) = addr` updates `gpr[ra]` (line 184). Because the repair does not reject `ra == rs`, `stdu` with `RA = RS != 0` stores the old `RS` value and updates `RA` to `EA`.
  50: 
  51: ### Q1(e) 64-bit-only instructions on 32-bit CPUs (`P7`, `D2`, `S9`, `S11`, `S12`, `R13`, `R17`)
  52: * **Audit of `P7` across [`X(to_be_translated)`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr.c#L4141-L5433) (`READ`)**:
  53:   * **Gated on `cpu->cd.ppc.bits == 32`**: Only `PPC_HI6_30` (`rld*`) at [cpu_ppc_instr.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr.c#L4602-L4606) (`READ`).
  54:   * **Ungated 64-bit-only instructions decoded in `X(to_be_translated)` (`READ`)**: `cmpdi`/`cmpldi` (`l_bit == 1` at `:4185`, `:4191`, `:4624`, `:4629`), `PPC_HI6_LD` (`:4307`), `PPC_HI6_STD` (`:4320`), `PPC_19_RFID` (`:4500`), `PPC_31_MTMSRD` (`:4705`), `PPC_31_LDARX` (`:4867`), `PPC_31_STDCX_DOT` (`:4869`), `PPC_31_STDX` (`:4921`), `PPC_31_STDUX` (`:4922`), `PPC_31_EXTSW` (`:5004`), and `PPC_31_SLD` (`:5006`).
  55:   * **Other 64-bit-only instructions (`READ`)**: `PPC_HI6_TDI` (`opcodes_ppc.h:61`) and `PPC_31_TD` (`opcodes_ppc.h:97`) are disassembled in `cpu_ppc.c:892, 958` (`READ`) but absent from `X(to_be_translated)` (hitting `default: goto bad;`); `ldx`, `ldux`, `lwax`, `lwaux`, `mulld`, `divd`, `srd`, `srad`, and `cntlzd` have no `PPC_31_*` defines in [opcodes_ppc.h](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/include/opcodes_ppc.h) (`READ`) and also fall into `default: goto bad;`.
  56: * **Choice between `(i)` and `(ii)` on `D2` (`DERIVED` under `R13`, `R17`)**: **Choose `(i)` - disclose in `NOT CLAIMED` (`C24`), do not add a `bits == 32` gate in this round** (consistent with Grok and `CRIT_RULINGS.md`).
  57:   * *Why*: Twelve 64-bit-only forms in `X(to_be_translated)` (including sibling X-form `stdx`, `stdux`, `ldarx`, `stdcx.`) are ungated on 32-bit CPUs (`P7`). Adding `if (cpu->cd.ppc.bits == 32) goto bad;` to opcodes 58/62 alone is outside the round's witness (`bareppc` / `PPC970`) and would leave `stdx`/`stdux` inconsistent, whereas gating all twelve belongs to a dedicated 32-bit-mode illegal-64-bit-opcode round (`R17`).
  58: 
  59: ### Q1(f) Alignment of `EA` (`P8`, `S14`)
  60: * **Verification of `P8` (`READ`)**: Opened [cpu_ppc_instr_loadstore.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr_loadstore.c#L41-L198) and [memory_ppc.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/memory_ppc.c#L254-L296). On 64-bit CPUs (`!cpu->is_32bit`), [`LS_N`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr_loadstore.c#L195-L198) always delegates to [`LS_GENERIC_N`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr_loadstore.c#L41-L186), which computes `uint64_t addr = reg(ic->arg[1]) + (int32_t)ic->arg[2];` and passes `addr` directly to `cpu->memory_rw` with `LS_SIZE` (`4` or `8`) and no alignment check (open items `#430`/`#431`). Even on 32-bit CPUs where the fast path checks `ofs & (LS_SIZE - 1)` ([cpu_ppc_instr_loadstore.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr_loadstore.c#L229)), an unaligned address simply falls back to `LS_GENERIC_N` (`:230`).
  61: * **Conclusion**: Nothing in the repair or its handlers assumes a 4- or 8-byte-aligned `EA` (`RA` may hold any byte address; the displacement `EXTS(DS || 0b00)` is always a multiple of 4). Using `BASE = 0x20080` in the probe is purely a test-data choice.
