  63: ### Q1(g) Disassembler folding in [`ppc_cpu_disassemble_instr`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc.c#L1468-L1601) (`P10`, `R16`, `R17`, `C25`)
  64: * **Verification of `P10` (`READ`)**: Opened [cpu_ppc.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc.c#L1468-L1601) and [debugger_cmds.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/debugger/debugger_cmds.c#L1837-L1947).
  65:   * At [cpu_ppc.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc.c#L1495-L1525), `ppc_cpu_disassemble_instr` computes `imm = (int16_t)(iword & 0xffff);`, assigns `mnem = "ld"` for `PPC_HI6_LD` (`:1498`) and `mnem = "std"` for `PPC_HI6_STD` (`:1517`), never inspects `iword & 3`, and prints `debug("%s\tr%i,%i(r%i)", mnem, rt, imm, ra)` (`:1532`). (Notably, `PPC_HI6_LFSU`, `LFDU`, `STFSU`, `STFDU` are also missing from the `case` list at `:1477-1489`!)
  66:   * When invoked from debugger `unassemble` (`cpu->running == 0`, [debugger_cmds.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/debugger/debugger_cmds.c#L1928)), `ppc_cpu_disassemble_instr` returns early at [cpu_ppc.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc.c#L1535-L1536) without touching guest memory. When invoked during live instruction tracing (`cpu->running == 1`), it performs a debug-only `cpu->memory_rw(..., MEM_READ, NO_EXCEPTIONS)` preview (`:1549-1550`) that does not alter guest registers or memory.
  67: * **Ruling (`R16`, `R17`)**: **File separately (do not fold into `#571`)**.
  68:   * Under `R17`, a second site in a different file ([cpu_ppc.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc.c)) with a guest-invisible cosmetic symptom (`LOW`) should not be bundled when doing so would invalidate the witness's green `unasm census` oracle (`R16`).
  69:   * With the disassembler filed separately, `regress/ppc_dsform_probe.py`'s `CONTRACT` must state explicitly under `OBSERVED` / `NOT CLAIMED` that `unasm census` verifies word placement (`opcd`, `RT`/`RS`, `RA`, and raw `DS || XO` halfword) against the tree's current `ld`/`std`-folding disassembler and **does not attest `XO` decode** (`C25`).
