  81: ## Q2 - Detector Row Set and Floor (`P9`, `P11`-`P15`, `C1`-`C26`, `R1`-`R11`, `R15`-`R19`)
  82: 
  83: ### Q2(a) Store half (`PPC_HI6_STD` = 62) (`P9`, `R1` clause (a))
  84: * **Verification of `P9` (`READ`)**: In [cpu_ppc_instr.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr.c#L4295-L4327) (`READ`), `case PPC_HI6_STD: size = 3; load = 0; break;` leaves `update = 0` and `imm = (int16_t)iword` for every `XO` $\in \{0,1,2,3\}$. Therefore on `BASE` (HEAD):
  85:   * `62/0` (`std`): stores 8 bytes of `RS` at `EA`, leaves `RA` unchanged (**GREEN** on `BASE`).
  86:   * `62/1` (`stdu`): stores 8 bytes of `RS` at `EA + 1` and leaves `RA` unchanged (**RED** on `BASE`).
  87:   * `62/1` (`stdu` with `RA = 0`, `C17`): stores 8 bytes of `RS` at absolute address `EXTS(DS || 01)` instead of `goto bad` (**RED** on `BASE`).
  88:   * `62/1` (`stdu` with `RA = RS != 0`, `C18`): stores 8 bytes of `RS` at `EA + 1` and leaves `RA` unchanged (**RED** on `BASE`).
  89:   * `62/2` and `62/3` (`C19`, `C20`): store 8 bytes of `RS` at `EA + 2` and `EA + 3` instead of `goto bad` (**RED** on `BASE`).
  90: * **Store rows and observables owed before the fix lands**:
  91:   1. **`std value` & `std RA after` (`C13`, control, `DS != 0`, e.g. `DS = -2`, `EA = BASE - 8`)**: store an 8-distinct-byte register value (e.g. `0xa0a1a2a3a4a5a6a7`) into a pre-seeded scratch region; verify via debugger `dump` that `MEM(EA, 8) == 0xa0a1a2a3a4a5a6a7` and neighbouring bytes `MEM(EA - 4, 4)` and `MEM(EA + 8, 4)` retain their pre-seeded background bytes, and verify `RA == BASE` (`std RA after`).
  92:   2. **`stdu value`, `stdu neigh`, & `stdu RA after` (`C15`, symptom, `DS != 0`, e.g. `DS = +4`, `EA = BASE + 16`)**: store an 8-distinct-byte value (e.g. `0xb0b1b2b3b4b5b6b7`); verify via debugger `dump` that `MEM(EA, 8) == 0xb0b1b2b3b4b5b6b7` (**RED** on `BASE`, where byte `EA` is still the background seed and `0xb0..b6` land at `EA+1..EA+7`), verify that neighbour window `MEM(EA + 8, 4)` retains its pre-seeded background (**RED** on `BASE`, where byte `EA + 8` is overwritten with `0xb7`), and verify `RA == EA` (`stdu RA after`, **RED** on `BASE` where `RA == BASE`).
  93:   3. **`stdu ds0 value` (`C16`, symptom, `DS = 0`, `EA = BASE`)**: store an 8-distinct-byte value at `DS = 0`; verify `MEM(BASE, 8)` holds the stored doubleword and `MEM(BASE + 8, 1)` is untouched (**RED** on `BASE`, which writes to `BASE + 1..BASE + 8`).
  94:   4. **`stdu alias value` & `stdu alias RA after` (`C18`, symptom, `RA = RS != 0`, `DS != 0`)**: with `rA = BASE`, execute `stdu rA, DS(rA)`; verify `MEM(EA, 8) == BASE` (old `rA`) and post-instruction `rA == EA` (**RED** on `BASE`).
  95:   5. **`stdu ra0 bad` (`C17`, symptom, `RA = 0`, in its own session)**: verify `"UNIMPLEMENTED instruction"` in transcript and target memory at `EXTS(DS || 01)` untouched (**RED** on `BASE`).
  96:   6. **`b62_2 bad` (`C19`) and `b62_3 bad` (`C20`, symptoms, each in its own session)**: verify `"UNIMPLEMENTED instruction"` in transcript, `RA == BASE`, and `MEM(EA, 12)` (covering `EA..EA+11`, which includes `EA+2..EA+9` and `EA+3..EA+10`) still equals the pre-seeded background (**RED** on `BASE`).
  97: 
  98: ### Q2(b) Reversing the fix (`P13`, `P15`, `R1` clause (b))
  99: * **Verification of `P13` and `P15` (`READ`)**: The repair touches only the displacement assignment and `case PPC_HI6_LD:` / `case PPC_HI6_STD:` in [cpu_ppc_instr.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr.c#L4295-L4327).
 100: * When HEAD's code is reinstated at those sites:
 101:   * In the main non-stopping session, HEAD never takes `goto bad` on any legal `ld`, `ldu`, `lwa`, `std`, or `stdu` with `RA != 0`, so the session runs all the way through `live` (`li r26, 0x42`), and every symptom row (`ldu value`, `ldu RA after`, `ldu ds0 value`, `lwa value`, `lwa pos value`, `lwa ds0 value`, `stdu value`, `stdu neigh`, `stdu RA after`, `stdu ds0 value`, `stdu alias value`, `stdu alias RA after`) fails on its own register/memory value while all controls (`ld`, `std`, `lwz`, `C21`, `C22`, `live`, `unasm census`, `neg apparatus`) stay GREEN (`CONTROL=OK`, `SYMPTOM=PRESENT`).
 102:   * In each of the five dedicated `goto bad` sessions (`C6`, `C12`, `C17`, `C19`, `C20`), placing the liveness `li` **before** the illegal word (`P15`) ensures that on the fixed build the liveness row is GREEN and the illegal word halts with `"UNIMPLEMENTED instruction"`, whereas on reinstated HEAD the illegal word executes as a shifted `ld`/`std` without halting, turning the session's `bad` row RED while its `live` row remains GREEN.
 103: 
 104: ### Q2(c) Clause (c) - Identity-body and dead-binary checks (`R2`)
 105: * **Medium & record form (`R2`)**: Run and record an **identity-body mutant** (`(c): measured at <artifact>`) in the pass-2 kill table-where `PPC_HI6_LD` and `PPC_HI6_STD` decode and advance `pc` without reading/writing memory or modifying `RT`/`RA`-plus state the by-construction dead-binary prediction:
 106:   * **On the identity-body mutant (`DERIVED`)**: Every register stays at `SENT` (`0x5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a`) or `BASE` (`0x20080`) and scratch memory stays at its pre-seeded pattern. Therefore:
 107:     * Controls `ld value` (`0x5a5a.. != 0x1011..`) and `std value` (background `!= 0xa0a1..`) go **RED**, flipping `PPC_DSFORM_CONTROL=FAIL`.
 108:     * Symptoms `ldu value`, `ldu RA after`, `ldu ds0 value`, `lwa value`, `lwa pos value`, `lwa ds0 value`, `stdu value`, `stdu RA after`, `stdu ds0 value`, `stdu alias value`, `stdu alias RA after`, and all five `goto bad` stop-transcript checks (`C6`, `C12`, `C17`, `C19`, `C20`) go **RED**.
 109:   * **On a dead binary (`READ` from [ppc_dsform_probe.py](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/ppcdsformxo/witness_20261024/ppc_dsform_probe.py#L444-L470))**:
 110:     * If the binary exits immediately without running debugger commands (`regs == {}`, `dis == []`), `unasm census` compares `"%d/%d" % (matched, len(dis))` (`"0/0"`) against `"%d/%d" % (N, N)` and goes **RED** (note: `unasm census` *does* depend on the emulator running `unassemble` in the main session, so it is only green on the identity-body mutant, not on a dead binary).
 111:     * On `/bin/false` (`exit 1` with empty output), `neg apparatus` (`"exit1/-0x1"`) is the sole row that can match (`1/N`), while `PPC_DSFORM_RESULT`, `PPC_DSFORM_CONTROL=FAIL`, and all `N-1` other rows fail; on `/bin/true` (`exit 0`), `neg apparatus` (`"exit0/-0x1" != "exit1/-0x1"`) also goes **RED** (`0/N`).
 112: 
 113: ### Q2(d) Partition of the input space and ruling on every `?` cell (`R3`-`R7`, `R18`, `R19`, `C1`-`C26`)
 114: * **Dominating and body-tested predicates in [`X(to_be_translated)`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr.c#L4269-L4352) (`READ`)**:
 115:   1. Outer and inner `switch (main_opcode)` over the 24 opcodes sharing the D/DS-form block (`:4269-4327`).
 116:   2. Inner `switch (iword & 3)` inside `PPC_HI6_LD` (`58`) and `PPC_HI6_STD` (`62`).
 117:   3. Shared tail predicates (`:4328-4351`): `ic->f == NULL` (`:4328`), `imm == 0` (`:4335`), `ra == 0 && update` (`:4338`), `fp` (`:4343`), and `ra == 0` (`:4347`).
 118: * **Ruling on every `?` cell in Section 7 (`C2`, `C3`, `C5`-`C7`, `C9`-`C11`, `C14`, `C16`-`C18`, `C21`-`C26`)**:
 119:   * **`C2` (`58/0 ld, DS=0`)**: **`(e)`** - for `XO = 0`, `(iword & ~3) == iword`, so `imm == 0` is identical pre- and post-fix.
 120:   * **`C3` (`58/0 ld, RA=0`)**: **`(e)`** - `update = 0` pre- and post-fix; `ra == 0` at `:4347` is untouched.
 121:   * **`C5` (`58/1 ldu, DS=0`)**: **FLOOR** (`R6`, `R7`, `P2`) - the shared body branches on `imm == 0` at `:4335`, where `DS = 0, XO = 1` has raw `imm = 1 != 0` vs. masked `imm = 0 == 0`. Distinguishes masking `imm` before `:4335` from masking only `ic->arg[2]` at `:4351` or masking only when `DS != 0`. (Channel: loaded value at `RA` vs `RA + 1`.)
 122:   * **`C6` (`58/1 ldu, RA=0`)**: **FLOOR** (`R6`, `R7`, `P5`) - the shared body branches on `if (ra == 0 && update) goto bad;` at `:4338`. Setting `update = 1` flips `(58/1, ra=0)` from a memory load at `EXTS(DS || 01)` to `goto bad`.
 123:   * **`C7` (`58/1 ldu, RA=RT != 0`)**: **`(e)`** (`D1`, `Q1(d)`) - `X(to_be_translated)` never compares `ra` with `rt`.
 124:   * **`C9` (`58/2 lwa, bit 31 CLEAR`)**: **FLOOR** (`D3`) - while bit 31 is a data bit inside `LS_GENERIC_N`, adding one positive-word `lwa` load (e.g. at `DATA + 0x08` where the word is `0x08090a0b`, bit 31 = 0 $\rightarrow$ `0x0000000008090a0b`) alongside negative `C8` (`0xffffffff88898a8b`) in the same session costs 1 instruction and kills any sign-extension mutant that unconditionally sets high bits `0..31`.
 125:   * **`C10` (`58/2 lwa, DS=0`)**: **FLOOR** (`R6`, `R7`, `P2`) - same body-tested `imm == 0` split at `:4335` as `C5` (`DS = 0, XO = 2` has raw `imm = 2 != 0` vs. masked `imm = 0`).
 126:   * **`C11` (`58/2 lwa, RA=0`)**: **`(e)`** - `update = 0` for `lwa`, so `ra == 0 && update` is false and `ra == 0` at `:4347` is unchanged by the diff.
 127:   * **`C14` (`62/0 std, DS=0 or RA=0`)**: **`(e)`** - same as `C2`/`C3` (`XO = 0`, `update = 0`).
 128:   * **`C16` (`62/1 stdu, DS=0`)**: **FLOOR** (`R6`, `R7`, `P2`) - same body-tested `imm == 0` split at `:4335` as `C5`/`C10` on opcode 62.
 129:   * **`C17` (`62/1 stdu, RA=0`)**: **FLOOR** (`R6`, `R7`, `P5`) - same body-tested `ra == 0 && update` split at `:4338` as `C6` on opcode 62.
 130:   * **`C18` (`62/1 stdu, RA=RS != 0`)**: **FLOOR** (`D3`) - kills a decoder mutant in `X(to_be_translated)` that mistakenly adds `if (ra == rs && update) goto bad;` across both 58 and 62, and costs 1 instruction in the store session.
 131:   * **`C21` (D-form LOAD with `D & 3 != 0`) & `C22` (D-form STORE with `D & 3 != 0`)**: **FLOOR** (`R18` dispatch-LABEL clause, `P14`) - all 24 opcodes in the arm share `imm = (int16_t)iword;` at `:4295`. Because the witness's only D-form row (`lwz` at `+8`) has `8 & 3 == 0` (`P14`), mutating line 4295 to `imm = (int16_t)(iword & ~3);` for all 24 opcodes would pass the witness undetected! One D-form load (`lwz` at `D = +6`, `6 & 3 == 2`) and one D-form store (`stw` at `D = +6`, `6 & 3 == 2`) are mandatory floor controls.
 132:   * **`C23` (D-form update forms & FP D-forms)**: **`(e)`** once `C21` and `C22` pin that `imm` at `:4295` is unmasked for non-58/62 opcodes (and Gate 13's [ppc_rounding_probe.py](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/ppc_rounding_probe.py#L79-L95) already exercises `lfs`/`lfsu`/`lfd`/`lfdu`/`stfs`/`stfsu`/`stfd`/`stfdu`/`stw`).
 133:   * **`C24` (58/62 on 32-bit CPU)**: **`(e)`** per `Q1(e)` option `(i)`.
 134:   * **`C25` (disassembler text for `ldu`/`lwa`/`stdu`)**: **`(e)`** per `Q1(g)` (filed separately).
 135:   * **`C26` (`ldu`/`stdu` whose memory access fails)**: **`(e)`** under `R5` (callee [`LS_GENERIC_N`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr_loadstore.c#L174) is outside `X(to_be_translated)`) and because on `bareppc` (`PPC970`), `MSR[DR]=0` identity-maps all addresses (`memory_ppc.c:258-261` `READ`) while `MSR[DR]=1` aborts at `fatal("TODO: ppc 64-bit translation\n")` ([memory_ppc.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/memory_ppc.c#L287-L288) `READ`, item `N3`).
 136: 
 137: ### Q2(e) Classifying the named variants and preserving non-target instructions (`P14`)
 138: 1. *"Displacement masked but `update` left 0 (`RA` unchanged)"*: **`(d)` null mutant** of the `update = 1` assignment on `58/1` (`ldu`) or `62/1` (`stdu`). Killed by `ldu RA after` (`C4`) and `stdu RA after` (`C15`) at `DS != 0`.
 139: 2. *"`update` set but raw `int16_t` kept (access at `EA + 1`)"*: **`(d)` null mutant** of the `imm & ~3` mask on `58/1` or `62/1`. Killed by `ldu value` (`C4`), `ldu RA after` (`C4`), `ldu ds0 value` (`C5`), `stdu value` (`C15`), `stdu RA after` (`C15`), and `stdu ds0 value` (`C16`).
 140: 3. *"`lwa` left at `size = 3` (neighbour word consumed)"*: **`(d)` null mutant** of `size = 2; zero = 0;` on `58/2`. Killed by `lwa value` (`C8`), `lwa pos value` (`C9`), and `lwa ds0 value` (`C10`).
 141: 4. *"A growth mutant that adds 1 to `XO=0` reds that row"* (or sets `update = 1` on `XO = 0` / `lwa`):
 142:    * Adding 1 to displacement on `XO = 0` is killed by `ld value` (`C1`) and `std value` (`C13`).
 143:    * **Important gap in the witness (`READ` at [ppc_dsform_probe.py](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/ppcdsformxo/witness_20261024/ppc_dsform_probe.py#L448-L452))**: In the witness, `r20` (`ld` base), `r22` (`lwa` base), and `r23` (`lwz` base) are only ungraded `obs()` lines, NOT graded `row()` assertions! A mutant that sets `update = 1` unconditionally for all legal `58/*` or `62/*` forms would pass `ld value`, `lwa value`, and `std value` unless `ld RA after` (`r20 == BASE`), `lwa RA after` (`r22 == BASE`), and `std RA after` (`RA == BASE`) are **graded rows** (at `DS != 0`). Promote those three `RA`-unchanged checks to rows.
 144: 5. **Instructions the repair must NOT change (`P14`)**:
 145:    * `58/0` (`ld`) and `62/0` (`std`): pinned by `C1` (`ld value` + `ld RA after`) and `C13` (`std value` + `std RA after`).
