## Q3 - detector shape and gate home

**(a) Sessions and header.** The script runs identically on both builds (R14(i); T36 precedent), so the session partition is a function of the **post-fix** disposition: every word that stops post-fix - 58/XO3, 62/XO2, 62/XO3 (CRIT: the existing `goto bad`) and `ldu`/`stdu` RA=0 (P5) - must be the **last** word of its own session, with a liveness word before it and nothing expected after (P15, S6). REASONED.

- **loads** session - the witness's (`ld` XO0, `ldu`, `lwa`, `lwz` control, `li` liveness). READ.
- **stores** session - new; own liveness (Grok 3.3: an `stw` of a known word); must contain no post-fix stopper, so 62/2, 62/3 and `stdu` RA=0 cannot share it.
- **five stop-word sessions** - 58/3, 62/2, 62/3, `ldu`-RA0, `stdu`-RA0, each liveness-first, stop-word last. (Count assumes C6/C17 are FLOOR; if the other firing rules them (e), drop two.)
- **32-bit session** only if the other firing adds a width test; the settled design does not (CRIT is silent; Grok D2 discloses) - shape would be 9.5's `bits32` rows.
- **census and neg apparatus.** Q3(a)'s own list omits the neg apparatus - the bogus-TYPE session that `CONTROL=OK` rests on (section 2); it must stay. The census must **grow** from 13/13 to every placed word: the store and illegal-XO words are the easiest to hand-assemble wrongly and are exactly the words a shared session cannot attest - and it must run **before any stop-word** or in its own invocation (P15: nothing after a stop runs). Its expectation stays today's folded text while the disassembler is unedited (settled design; P13's disassembler lines are conditional on Q1(g)).

Seven sessions minimum (P15 also lets a stop-word take the last slot of a green session, census before it), nine with census and neg as separate invocations. Order otherwise free; neg apparatus last (witness shape); sentinel last.

Header changes: CONTRACT drops "no store instruction is placed in the guest" and moves 58/3, 62/2, 62/3 and the RA=0 update words from NOT COVERED to claimed; NOT CLAIMED keeps RA=RT (D1, disclosed), 32-bit (if disclosed), translation/SF/page-crossing/indexed forms, the disassembler text if filed. SYMPTOM grows from the three load reds to include store and stop rows, and the gated run pins ABSENT (9.2). Per R10 the header names the edits it is built to catch - P13's three decoder lines.

Structural note vs S16: #570's witness and detector were byte-identical; here the frozen witness is loads-only and the detector is a superset. So the CLASS_WITNESS artifact attests the **load half only**; the store half's clause-(a) red is a *separate* artifact - the grown detector's run on base HEAD, preserved like `prefix_HEAD.out`. This feeds Q3(e).

**(b)** Gate 13, after the `#565` rldicl block, before `need_file "$IMAGES/netbsd401-macppc-GENERIC"`. READ (S15, 9.1): the three register probes already run on the witness's exact machine (`-E bareppc -M 64`) with only `need_exec "$PMAX"` and the python3 check ahead; the new block inherits those two and costs nothing new. Placed after `need_file`, it would inherit the image skip - a real cost on an imageless host. Gate 14 is precedented for cross-arch hosting (#570 is m88k in gate_arm) but strictly worse: eleven earlier skip points (9.2) against two. REASONED.

**(c)** Two lines, right in substance, with one reconciliation. DERIVED: the MANIFEST lists #570's detector as a bare filename for a file at `regress/` (9.3 vs S16), so MANIFEST paths resolve regress/-relative - the WITNESS line should read `artifacts/ppcdsformxo/witness_20261024/ppc_dsform_probe.py` - while the ledger cites root-relative `regress/...` paths (the state note's own citations), so Q3(e)'s form belongs there. Both forms are right in their own contexts; the records should say which resolver each follows, because a MANIFEST path that does not resolve is a wrong record. NOT CHECKABLE: (i) the witness script's actual filename - section 2 never names it (Q3(c)/(e) assume `ppc_dsform_probe.py`); use the real name if it differs. (ii) The checker's join rule - settling fact: how `check_probe_wiring.py` resolves paths (or #570's on-disk witness path). Kill-table frozen copies: yes, `*.py.txt`/`*.sh.txt` per #570 (9.3). `ppc_dsform_dummy.bin` is not a `.py`; the prefix run's output is an `.out`; nothing else the checker would see is nameable from the packet.

**(d)** Adopt the #570 shape wholesale; the `%-16s` column, 15-char assert and duplicate-name assert (9.6) already make `^$v  .*ok$` = 1 sound. Add: (1) a liveness row per session - **required** in any session containing a stop-word (9.5 precedent: `bits32 live` before `bits32 rld bad`); the by-name counts prove a row printed, not that the session reached its stop-word in order; recommended in every session since the detector is multi-session. (2) Pin `PPC_DSFORM_RED=` - the line already exists (section 2, line 8) - to its no-red literal, exactly once; redundant with the per-row counts for catching a red, but an unpinned summary line is drift room. (3) Pin the census row's halves (13/13  N/N) as RESULT's are pinned. Optionally pin `PROBE_RC` 0; sentinel+counts suffice. Gate 13's `#565` idiom (SCORE line) and the #570 additions are compatible.

**(e)** Rung 3 is right (READ, section 2). Path form right (DERIVED, (c)). Two gaps: (i) the `probe:` term's syntax is NOT CHECKABLE - no witnessed ledger row is inlined; settle by copying #570's term verbatim. (ii) The single term must not be readable as covering the store half: the frozen witness is loads-only **by its own contract** (section 2), and the store reds come from the grown detector's pre-fix run (see (a)). The state note must scope the term to the loads and name the store-half prefix artifact, or the term overclaims. Both the term and the MANIFEST line land only when the directory is committed (section 2: uncommitted).

**(f)** Blast radius: the shared `imm` line (4295  4351) and the two case lines - all 24 arm opcodes pass through them; the eight FP D-forms set `ic->f` themselves and skip only the table index (8.2). READ. Consumers: the rounding probe's FP rows (`lfs`/`stfs`/`lfd`/`stfd` + update forms - Q3(f)'s text) are IN the arm and must re-run green - but that block is image-gated, so on an imageless host the FP forms' coverage vanishes. The three register probes' under-test instructions are not among S2's 24 load/store labels, and the only inlined fragment (9.5) shows `li`, also outside the arm; whether their scaffolding places D-form words is NOT CHECKABLE (guest listings not inlined). The NetBSD boot behind the image check is the broad integer-D-form consumer. Consequence to record: before the image check, nothing in gate 13 exercises the integer D-forms except the new probe's own rows - and the witness's `lwz` control uses +8, low bits 00 (P14), so as shipped it cannot catch an over-broad mask (whether C21/C22 close that is Q2(e)'s call). Re-run gate 13 in full; PowerPC D-form rigs outside it: NOT CHECKABLE (the packet names none).

## Q4 - the standing licence

**(1) Disassembler fold - REAL.** READ: 8.9 takes `imm = (int16_t)(iword & 0xffff)` (1495), prints `ld`/`std` for every opcode-58/62 word (1498, 1517), no XO test; the census shows it (`ld r5,-95(r21)` for the `ldu` word, `ld r6,10(r22)` for `lwa`). Guest-invisible confirmed from 8.9: `if (!running) break` (1535) precedes all address work, and the running=1 preview is a NO_EXCEPTIONS read - nothing is written. Severity strictly below T2's: no guest state, no crash - a diagnostics defect (wrong mnemonic, wrong displacement, wrong previewed address, `<0x20021>`). The queue's class label for a non-guest defect is NOT CHECKABLE; I would file LOW. Witness: none new owed - the census on unmodified HEAD *is* the reproduction; cite witness_20261024's OBS rows. Out of #571 under R17: repairing it changes the census oracle, so "same detector, no new oracle" fails - matching the settled design, which is silent on it.

**(2) `ldx`/`ldux`/`lwax`/`lwaux` - REAL per S12** (settled; nothing in the packet contradicts it). Effect: a CPU stop (S6), no delivery, no corruption - a different semantic class from T2's GUEST-CORRUPTION. "Already filed under another name": NOT CHECKABLE - the packet carries only `ppcdsformxo`'s row and queue line 33; the drafter's negative grep is asserted, not shown. Settling fact: the full ledger/OUTSTANDING_BUGS title list at HEAD. Scope: OUT of #571 under R17 - not witnessed, different semantic class, no shared fix design (the DS mask does nothing for opcode-31 X-form arms), new oracle required. File as its own row, recording the aggravating asymmetry (`stdx`/`stdux` implemented, the indexed loads absent); the natural rung-3 witness, when its round comes, is a one-session stepped probe placing an `ldx` word on HEAD PPC970.

**(3) Found while verifying:** (i) Q3(a)'s session list omits the negative control (restored above). (ii) Section 12's "every repository path cited exists at HEAD" is false as stated for the witness paths - section 2 says the witness directory is *uncommitted*, so those paths exist in the working tree, not at HEAD; harmless because Q3(c) conditions the MANIFEST line on committing, but the blanket sentence should not be read as covering them.
